THIRD-PARTY AND PRIOR RIGHTS
---------------------------

This project is an independent homage to *Elite* (1984), created by David Braben and Ian
Bell. Rights in *Elite* — including its name, universe, ship designs, and related
intellectual property — rest with their respective owners (Frontier Developments and the
original authors). The copyright claimed above extends only to this project's own original
code, text, and generated artwork. It asserts no rights over *Elite* itself and is not
endorsed by, affiliated with, or approved by its rights holders.

No assets were extracted from any original *Elite* binary. All geometry, text, and artwork
here are recreated from published specifications and public documentation.

Third-party components are used under their own licences and are not covered by the terms
above. Three.js is distributed under the MIT Licence; see web/vendor/ for the bundled copy.


NOTE
----

This file is a starting point, not legal advice. Two things remain open and are tracked in
product.md §15:

  1. The IP question (§15 Q1) is explicitly marked as blocking public release. Publishing
     this project publicly is the action that question was written to gate.

  2. If the project is ever released under different terms — non-commercial homage,
     licensed remake, or a renamed "serial numbers filed off" version — this file must be
     revisited to match that decision.
